 "invariants": [
  "Replay resolves an original input ID on the current pi branch.",
  "Replay retains original content and immutable attachment claims while current authorization is revalidated.",
  "Admission cleanup only removes the exact captured composer references.",
  "A completed queue cancellation retains every original text, skill and attachment claim even if some media no longer resolves; unresolved media remains visible and blocks send until the user removes or replaces it.",
  "Conversation commands retain their captured workspace, lane and pi session through every async wait; project identity alone never authorizes another conversation.",
  "Recovered drafts are window-local input buffers keyed by immutable project UUID and pi session; late cancellation never borrows another project resolver or merges into its current composer.",
  "Restored selectors are carried separately; admission surface, model and policy come from this send, never historical input.",
  "The complete composer revision spans text, skills, templates, attachments and references; late cancellation auto-restores only an unchanged empty buffer.",
  "A synchronous admission token prevents duplicate sends and buffer swaps until ACK; successful cleanup is atomic and cannot bank an accepted input as unsent.",
  "Upload settlement follows the original attachment ID and immutable project owner across recovered buffer swaps; stale results never mutate another project composer."
 ],
